  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "summary": "Every application log record and CLI error is one newline-delimited JSON envelope, including service, upstream handshake, and HTTP lane records"
    },
    {
      "id": "R2",
      "summary": "Application-owned envelope fields are schema_version, level, service, event, message, operation, outcome, nested error, config/resource objects, typed entry fields, and the closed AD8 vocabulary"
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "summary": "The application never emits timestamps, subsystem, container identity, host, environment, or version"
    },
    {
      "id": "R4",
      "summary": "debug/info to stdout, warn/error to stderr; one JSON object per line, one write, no retry, no plaintext fallback"
    },
    {
      "id": "R5",
      "summary": "Nested error carries code, kind, retryable, remediation; message is human-only; the HTTP lane uses the same nested shape"
    },
    {
      "id": "R6",
      "summary": "Configuration diagnostics carry path, property path, one-based line and column, safe identifiers, and related location, with documented position exceptions"
    },
    {
      "id": "R7",
      "summary": "Pin ceiling reports pins[64] at its document-order position with validated identity only, plus counts and first excess index"
    },
    {
      "id": "R8",
      "summary": "No record serializes secret values, URLs, query strings, headers, payloads, raw YAML, or arbitrary Go error text"
    },
    {
      "id": "R9",
      "summary": "Fail-fast: first error in deterministic document order, exactly one detailed event, no summary event"
    },
    {
      "id": "R10",
      "summary": "Startup rejection is error with exit 1; reload rejection is warn and retains the active configuration"
    },
    {
      "id": "R11",
      "summary": "Non-configuration failures use the same envelope with stable codes, kinds, retryability, remediation, and safe resources"
    },
    {
      "id": "R12",
      "summary": "--help stays human-readable and emits no JSON record"
    },
    {
      "id": "R13",
      "summary": "Validation success emits config_validation_succeeded with no error object and no configuration contents"
    },
    {
      "id": "R14",
      "summary": "Exit code for configuration failure stays 1"
    },
    {
      "id": "R15",
      "summary": "No panic recovery; Go crash report untouched (non-goal)"
    },
    {
      "id": "R16",
      "summary": "No raw-cause diagnostic mode (non-goal)"
    },
    {
      "id": "R17",
      "summary": "No legacy aliases: time, environment, version, flat reason, flat error.class are removed with consumers and docs migrated"
    },
    {
      "id": "R18",
      "summary": "schema_version starts at 1; breaking field changes increment it; optional additions do not"
    },
    {
      "id": "R19",
      "summary": "Docker Compose log prefix is orchestrator output; the application does not work around it (non-goal)"
    },
    {
      "id": "R20",
      "summary": "Pins are mandatory: an unresolved mandatory pin rejects the candidate catalog while the previously published catalog keeps serving, and every pin-failure record states whether it blocked publication or left a degraded candidate publishable (owner rulings 1, 5)."
    },
    {
      "id": "R21",
      "summary": "A failed pin check reports every unresolved pin, each with safe server/tool identity and configuration source location; discovery-failed pins are reported unverifiable, never tool-absent; discovered tool names are listed for affected servers only, chunked without silent truncation; every failed pass repeats complete details (owner rulings 2, 3, 4, 13)."
    },
    {
      "id": "R22",
      "summary": "Logs alone are the diagnostic path: start and outcome records share one refresh correlation id and state the configuration revision, trigger and next attempt; a failed pass distinguishes the retained catalog from no usable catalog and candidate counts from retained counts; a successful pass reports counts only (owner rulings 6, 7, 11, 12, 14, 15)."
    },
    {
      "id": "R23",
      "summary": "An upstream discovery failure names the failing stage from the closed set dns|connect|tls|auth|initialize|tools_list with a bounded cause and HTTP status or timeout; the endpoint is sanitized to scheme, host, port and path; each failure states retry-scheduled versus correction-required with the next attempt (owner rulings 8, 9)."
    },
    {
      "id": "R24",
      "summary": "The log shows a configuration edit reaching the running process: reload attempts identify the revision and trigger and whether the candidate was accepted or rejected, and refresh records name the revision they used (owner rulings 10, 18)."
    },
    {
      "id": "R25",
      "summary": "Pin and refresh diagnostics appear at default log levels; no failure diagnostic is debug-only; defects in the logging path itself are surfaced as a minimal credential-free fallback (owner rulings 16, 17)."
    }
  ],
